# S199's WITNESS. Without it that row has an EMPTY population and scores
# UNDETECTED: MEASURED, all 59 distinct `features` lists in the corpus
# are valid, so a plant that makes run.sh silently ACCEPT an invalid one
# has nothing to accept.
#
# The failure this pins is nastier than it looks. pcrec refuses an
# unknown module name with exit 1 — which is exactly what a `perr` block
# asserts. So a typo'd `features` line makes the block below PASS while
# testing nothing about the pattern: it certifies that pcrec rejected a
# FEATURES SPEC, not that it rejected the regex. run.sh must therefore
# validate the list itself and fail LOUDLY, which is what this file
# checks and what S199 removes.
pattern (?<n>a)\k<n>
features bogus_module_name
perr
